.TH EUCLID-CLI-ENS-CREATE-TOPIC 1 "August 2026" "euclid-cli 1.18.37" "Euclid CLI Manual"
.SH NAME
euclid-cli-ens-create-topic \- create a new notification topic
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B euclid-cli ens create-topic
.BR \-\-name | \-n
.I NAME
[\fB\-\-max\-length\fR|\fB\-l\fR \fIBYTES\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Creates a new topic with the given name and maximum message length.
.PP
The topic is created in the caller's own account and region (taken from
the logged-in session, not given on the command line). The created
topic's name and Euclid resource name (ERN) are printed as JSON.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-name " " \fINAME\fR
Name of the topic to create. Required.
.TP
.BR \-l ", " \-\-max\-length " " \fIBYTES\fR
Maximum message body length, in bytes. Defaults to \fI1048576\fR (1 MiB).
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The topic was created; its ERN is printed as JSON.
.TP
.B 1
Missing/invalid arguments, the server could not be reached, or the
server rejected the request (e.g. a topic with that name already
exists).
.SH EXAMPLES
.RS
.nf
euclid-cli --endpoint http://localhost:5566 ens create-topic \e
    --name order-events

euclid-cli --endpoint http://localhost:5566 ens create-topic \e
    --name order-events --max-length 65536
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR euclid-cli-ens (1),
.BR euclid-cli-ens-list-topics (1),
.BR euclid-cli-ens-get-topic-ern (1),
.BR euclid-cli-ens-delete-topic (1)
